Beef Wellington
Serves: 8
Prep: 40 min
Cook: 1½ hr
Total: 3 hr 40 min
Equipment: Butcher's twine, Cast-iron skillet, 12″ skillet, Small skillet, Food processor, Plastic wrap, Rolling pin, Rimmed baking sheet, Foil, Instant-read thermometer, Serrated knife

Carve: Loosen from foil, move to board. Slice off ends, then carve with a serrated knife. Chives and salt on the cut faces.
  Bake (heat, 35–45 min): **220 °C / 425 °F**, foil-lined sheet. Egg-wash, score, salt. Bake to **43 °C** rare / **49 °C** medium-rare at the centre. Rest **10 min**.
    Wrap (combine, 30 min): Unwrap; foie side up on pastry edge. Egg-wash **15 cm** above, roll, seam under. Fold, trim and seal ends. Chill **≥30 min**.
      Roll (combine, 30 min): Beef on bottom edge, foie slices on top. Roll tight using the wrap. Re-wrap, twist ends. Chill **≥30 min**.
        Coat (then chill): Mix horseradish, mustard and pepper. Once beef is cool, cut off twine and rub all over. Fridge, **uncovered**.
          Sear (heat, ~10 min): Oil **smoking**, high heat. Brown each side without moving, ~2 min a side.
            Tie: Trim off silverskin and loose fat. Tie with twine at **2.5 cm** intervals. Season liberally.
              - 900 g = 2 lb | Beef tenderloin | centre-cut
              - to taste | Kosher salt & pepper | liberally
            - 2 Tbsp | Vegetable oil
          - 2 Tbsp | Prepared horseradish
          - 1 Tbsp | Mustard | Dijon or hot English
          - 1 tsp | Black pepper
        Layer (combine): Phyllo on double plastic wrap (60×30 cm). Shingle prosciutto, leaving **5 cm** top and bottom. Spread duxelles over.
          Split (combine, 30 min): Stir foie **fat into duxelles**. Halve each foie slab horizontally. Chill duxelles, foie and beef **≥30 min**.
            Reduce (heat, ~8 min): Brandy in, scrape fond, cook until **nearly dry**. Add cream and soy; cook until it **holds as one mass**. Season. Fridge.
              Brown (heat, ~14 min): Medium-high until liquid is gone, then until **fond** sticks. Add shallots and thyme for the last **2 min**.
                Pulse: Roughly chop. Food processor in **two batches**, ~10 short pulses each, until very fine.
                  - 450 g = 1 lb | Mushrooms | any mix
                - 55 g = 4 Tbsp | Unsalted butter
                Chop: Finely dice the shallots. Strip the thyme leaves and mince finely.
                  - 2 | Shallots
                  - 4–5 sprigs | Fresh thyme | for 2 tsp leaves
              - 120 ml = ½ cup | Cognac | or bourbon
              - 120 ml = ½ cup | Heavy cream
              - 2 tsp | Soy sauce
              - to taste | Salt & pepper
            Sear (heat, 1 min): Cut into two **1 cm** slabs; season. Small skillet, oil **smoking**, **30 s** a side. Drain on paper towel.
              - 115 g | Fresh foie gras | or pâté: slice, skip sear
              - to taste | Salt & pepper | liberally
              - ½ tsp | Vegetable oil
          - 1 sheet | Phyllo dough
          - 115 g = ¼ lb | Prosciutto | paper-thin
      Roll out (then set aside): If frozen, thaw in the fridge **overnight**. Roll to a rectangle **10 cm wider** than the beef roll on its short side.
        - for dusting | Flour
        - 400 g = 14 oz | Puff pastry | all-butter
      Beat: Beat with a fork. Use half to seal; keep half for the glaze.
        - 1 | Egg
    - ½ | Beaten egg | kept from Beat
    - to taste | Flaky sea salt | Maldon
  Mince: Slice very finely.
    - 1 bunch | Chives
  - to taste | Flaky sea salt
